.TH "SPP-ENV-MODE" 1 "November 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
spp-env-mode \- Switch environment profile, error reporting mode, and internal system portals between dev and prod
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spp env:mode
<\fIdev\fR|\fIprod\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B env:mode
switches the global operational profile between development (\fBdev\fR) and production (\fBprod\fR).
In development mode, ignition error pages are enabled, and internal protected system portals (\fBsppadmin\fR and \fBsppdev\fR) are fully active.
In production mode, user-facing 500 error pages are served, and system administration portals are disabled with HTTP 403 Forbidden responses to protect production servers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR <dev|prod>
Target environment mode. Required.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
.IP \(bu 2
Modifies \fIspp/etc/global-settings.yml\fR (\fBprofile\fR and \fBdebug\fR flags).
.IP \(bu 2
Synchronizes \fIspp/etc/settings.xml\fR profile node.
.IP \(bu 2
Unlinks and purges compiled configuration cache in \fIvar/cache/system/config.php\fR.
